### Decisions

These are built into the toolkit. Change them in the toolkit so every server stays the same.

1. Tarball installs, not RPMs, for Mattermost, rtcd, OpenSearch and the monitoring tools. Each
   version gets its own directory under `/opt` and a symlink points at the live one, so upgrades and
   rollbacks are a symlink swap. PostgreSQL and Nginx come from RHEL AppStream so they get RHEL errata.
2. Every downloaded artifact is checked against the vendor checksum, and Mattermost and OpenSearch
   also against their GPG signatures. Trust comes from keys and fingerprints held in this repo, not
   from the download source.
3. Mattermost config lives in `{{ mattermost_config_dir }}`, outside the install directory, and we merge
   only the keys we own. Admins can still use the System Console for everything else.
4. Services that only local components use bind to 127.0.0.1 and get no firewall opening. Remote
   access is opt-in per component, by source address.
5. SELinux stays enforcing and firewalld stays on. Where fapolicyd runs, we add trust entries for our
   install directories instead of turning it off.
6. OpenSearch uses certificates from its own CA, never the demo certificates that ship with it.
7. Block storage and object storage are out of scope. Uploaded files go to local disk, to an NFS
   share this toolkit can serve (the `storage` profile), or to an S3 bucket you provide.

