{% if has.mm %}
### Upgrade Mattermost

Re-runs keep the installed version{{ ' even though the channel is ' ~ mattermost_version_channel if mattermost_version_channel != 'pinned' else '' }}. To upgrade:

1. Take a file backup of the uploaded files{{ ' in `' ~ mattermost_data_dir ~ '`' if mattermost_file_driver == 'local' else '' }}.
2. Run `./install.sh --answers ... --upgrade` to move to the newest release on the channel, or pin a newer `mattermost_version` and re-run.
3. Mattermost stops, the database is dumped to `{{ mattermost_backup_dir }}` with a copy of `config.json`{{ '' if mattermost_upgrade_backup | bool else ' (switched off here: `mattermost_upgrade_backup` is false, so take your own first)' }}, the new version unpacks to `{{ mattermost_install_root }}/mattermost-<version>`, the symlink moves and Mattermost starts. The old directory stays put.

The installer refuses to install an older version than the one running. Database migrations only
go forwards, so rolling back means restoring the dump from step 3 (`pg_restore --clean`), then
pointing `{{ mattermost_dir }}` back at the old directory and restarting.

{% endif %}
